<title>UK: SOCCER-LITTLE SUPPORTED TO SUCCEED KEEGAN.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LITTLE SUPPORTED TO SUCCEED KEEGAN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bookmakers were swift to name Kenny</p>
<p>Dalglish on Wednesday as odds on favourite to succeed Kevin</p>
<p>Keegan as manager of Newcastle, but William Hill reported some</p>
<p>early support for Aston Villa's Brian Little and cut his odds</p>
<p>from 33-1 to 16-1.</p>
<p>Latest betting:</p>
<p>4-5 Kenny Dalglish</p>
<p>4-1 John Toshack</p>
<p>8-1 Johan Cruyff, Terry McDermott</p>
<p>12-1 Bobby Robson, Chris Waddle</p>
<p>16-1 Brian Little</p>
<p>33-1 Jackie Charlton</p>
</text>
